A1. Name a small descendant of Eve's traducer. ~ ASP
A4. What should tired business men do with their evenings? ~ SLEEP
A8. What is the call of the Charleston? ~ HEY
A11. What does Reuben lose when he tries a shell game? ~ PEA
A13. What is Volstead's farce called? ~ ACT
A14. Name something precious to most women. ~ GEM
A16. What Biblical character was stoned? ~ STEPHEN
A19. What word pertains to every bonehead? ~ CRANIAL
A22. What is the call of the inebriate? ~ HIC
A23. What is the big stick of today? ~ ALCOHOL
A25. What means just nothing at all? ~ NIL
A26. What abbreviation is used to mean "others of a kind"? ~ ETC
A28. What do American fliers possess? ~ MERIT
A29. What did Nurmi usually do when he ran? ~ LED
A31. What do most people do when they should reduce? ~ EAT
A33. What comes between nine and eleven o'clock on Sunday evenings? ~ TEN
A34. Name an indolent tumor of the skin. ~ WEN
A36. What kind of people often give you a trimming? ~ BARBERS
A39. What is the comparative degree of a word meaning big, famous? ~ GREATER
A42. What little word means "in like manner"? ~ AS
A43. Name a part of the verb "to be." ~ ARE
A44. What insect has a reputation for hard work? (Not your old man.) ~ ANT
A45. Name a note in the scale. ~ LA
A46. What are Judge, Jr. enthusiasts troubled with? (Plural.) ~ THIRSTS
A49. What does divorce do to the chains of matrimony? ~ UNCHAIN
A51. Where does the golf dub's trouble start? ~ TEE
A52. What is dix to a Frenchman? ~ TEN
A54. What is there about women's dresses that comes higher each year? ~ HEM
A55. What is the bar sinister to the feminine figure? ~ FAT
A56. Give another name for a fine or penalty. ~ MULCT
A58. Name a primary color. ~ RED
A60. What is it to feel pain or trouble? ~ AIL
A61. What is a tiresome movie? ~ TEDIOUS
A63. What is it to seek alms with firearms? ~ ROB
A65. What is the title of a high church official? ~ PRIMATE
A67. What is useful? ~ UTILITY
A69. What is it we have around us all the time? ~ AIR
A70. What catches many a poor fish? ~ NET
A72. Give the name of a fabulous bird of prey. ~ ROC
A73. Name a much used little conjunction. ~ AND
A74. How did the doughboy feel in the trenches? ~ ITCHY
A75. What force runs the machinery of government? ~ GAS

D2. Name something frightful. ~ SPECTER
D3. What did Mr. Babbitt put into his business? ~ PEP
D5. What instruments are useful to surgeons? ~ LANCETS
D6. What is there between England and France? (Init.) ~ EC
D7. What makes many an artist scratch? ~ ETCHING
D8. What is always laying around the farm? ~ HEN
D9. What people walk in paths of glory? ~ EMINENT
D10. Name a tree of the olive family. ~ ASH
D12. Give an exclamation of delight. ~ AHA
D14. What is a backwoods maiden called by her pappy? ~ GAL
D15. If three cops raided a speakeasy, how many would take a drink? ~ ALL
D17. What is usually hanging around a movie hero's neck? ~ TIE
D18. Name something shady. ~ ELM
D20. What do you find in the Tabloids? ~ ROT
D21. What is it to give assistance? ~ AID
D24. Name something unrefined. ~ ORE
D27. Where do high steppers step? ~ CABARET
D29. What is usually seen around the dogs? ~ LEATHER
D30. What does it mean to diminish? ~ ABATE
D32. How do you like after-dinner speeches? ~ TERSE
D34. What is often met at the village post-office? ~ WENCH
D35. What fell awhile ago in France? ~ FRANC
D37. Name a kind of tree. ~ ASH
D38. What word means to seep, or soak? ~ RET
D40. What did Zev do to win fame? ~ RAN
D41. What do Yale boys play football for? ~ ELI
D47. What people live in a country shaped like a boot? ~ ITALIAN
D48. What is hard to find during football season at any university? ~ STUDENT
D49. What is New Jersey society to New York society? ~ UNCOUTH
D50. Name something which never dries up. ~ AMERICA
D53. What name is associated with New Haven, Conn.? ~ ELI
D55. Name something ever green. ~ FIR
D56. What did a famous conference do in Geneva? ~ MET
D57. Who was made famous by his mummy? ~ TUT
D59. What goes with a dash? ~ DOT
D60. What flits from limb to limb? ~ APE
D61. What is often at sea? ~ TAR
D62. Name a title of respect. ~ SIR
D64. What word means "of secondary importance"? ~ BYE
D66. What denotes the middle position? ~ MID
D68. What kind of houses were great men of the last generation born in? ~ LOG
D71. What is an abbreviation for Established Church? ~ EC


